clueweb09-en0006-55-08139.75 Friends of the Sherwood Regional Library - FCPL the motto of the Friends of the Sherwood Regional Library. The group is active in enhancing library services by supporting library programs, outreach, the volunteer program and the purchase of equipment for the branch. In addition to activities in the branch, the Friends have partnered with the Reading Is Fundamental program to provide free books to children at the local affordable health center. To become a Friend of the Sherwood Regional Library, please complete this online form. Friends Choice Award Recipients October 20, 2008 Dorothea Bruckner Pier Penic Liz Promen Mission Statement: The purpose of the Friends of the Sherwood
clueweb09-en0006-55-08018.0 Sherwood Regional Library - FCPL [Fairfax County, Virginia] [Fairfax County] Search Site: Home Living Here Doing Business Visiting Departments & Agencies [*] Sherwood Regional Library [*] homepage > library > branches > sherwood regional library [*] Home Account Services Research Tools Catalog Databases Events Library Branches Good Reading About the Library Site Index [Sherwood Regional Library.]2501 Sherwood Hall Lane Alexandria, VA 22306-2799 Telephone: 703-765-3645 TTY: 711 or 703-324-8365 The Sherwood Regional Library has been serving residents of the historic Mount Vernon District since 1971. The library's collections and services reflect the diverse population in the area. A computer lab and a varied program of free,
clueweb09-en0006-55-08018.75 Sherwood Regional Library - FCPL Vernon District since 1971. The library's collections and services reflect the diverse population in the area. A computer lab and a varied program of free, hands-on technology courses helps community members across the digital divide. An active Friends of the Library group provides programming for all ages, including literature programs for adults and professional performers for children. An extensive volunteer program offers a wide selection of choices for citizens wishing to share their talents with the community. Our New Books | Events Directions | Public Transportation | Library Closing Dates Library Hours of Operation Sunday Monday Tuesday Wednesday Thursday Friday
