clueweb09-en0006-55-08251.75 Group Study Rooms - FCPL for use by small groups working together on projects that require a level of interaction that might be distracting to other library users. These rooms are available at no charge for use by organizations and individuals for educational, cultural and informational community meetings and programs. They are available during regular operating hours. Reservations may be made by contacting your local library branch. Reservations are accepted on a first-come, first-served basis. Group study room rules and guidelines Reservations may be made for the current seven days. The maximum number of reservations per group is two per current seven days. Groups may
