clueweb09-enwp03-18-10568.0 Sherwood Forest (neighborhood) - Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia Sherwood Forest (neighborhood) From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia Jump to: navigation, search Sherwood Forest [] Country United States State North Carolina County Mecklenburg City Charlotte Population (March 16, 2008) - Total 1,381 according to Zillow.com ZIP code The Sherwood Forest neighborhood of Charlotte, North Carolina was established in the 1950s. In addition to the Sherwood Forest subdivision, the area also includes the Castleton Gardens and Charlestowne Manor subdivisions. The area is bisected by McMullen Creek and is neighbored by the areas known as East Forest, Stonehaven, Landsdowne, Providence Park, and Cotswold. The area's dominant architectural style is the ranch-style house
clueweb09-enwp03-18-10568.75 Sherwood Forest (neighborhood) - Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia and is neighbored by the areas known as East Forest, Stonehaven, Landsdowne, Providence Park, and Cotswold. The area's dominant architectural style is the ranch-style house with brick or wood exterior. In keeping with its namesake, some of the area's street names (such as Nottingham Dr. and Robinhood Rd.) are attributed to characters and places in the Robin Hood stories. [edit] External links Sherwood Forest on Google maps Sherwood Forest quality of life profile v ýýý d ýýý e City of Charlotte, North Carolina Main Charlotteans ýý Mecklenburg County ýý Metrolina ýý North Carolina ýý Piedmont Government Mayor Pat McCrory ýý
