clueweb09-en0010-99-34210.75 SALINE COUNTY LIBRARY - Gateway Policies About the Library Library Holidays Staff & Board Library History A Collection-sharing program for libraries in Central Arkansas About the Program [gatewaymap] The Gateway Project provides public library service to Central Arkansas residents with-out charging a non-resident fee to patrons outside a library's service area. The program was initiated in 1995 as a succesful LSDA DEvelopment grant for library patrons in Cleveland, Conway, Dallas, Faulkner, Grant, Hot Spring, Lonoke, Perry, Prarie, Pulaski, Saline, Van Buren and White counties. The program has expanded to include Arkansas, Garland, Jackson, Jefferson, Pike and Pope counties. 56 libraries in these counties currently participate
