clueweb09-en0003-01-26802.75 Archive of Features About the Yellowstone Volcanic System Archive Archive of Features About the Yellowstone Volcanic System 2007 University of Utah scientists publish long-term study of crustal motions of the Yellowstone Hotspot 03/08/2007 University of Utah graduate student Christine Puskas, along with YVO coordinating scientist Bob Smith and others, recently published a long-term study of crustal movements associated with the Yellowstone hotspot. This technical article summarizes 17 years of Global Positioning System (GPS) data acquired to understand how the Yellowstone volcano and the Snake River Plain volcanic field interacts with the nearby Teton and Hebgen Lake faults and the tectonic system of the Western U.S. The original paper,
