clueweb09-en0003-57-14820.75 Yellowstone National Park Site 1978 [Historical poster of Yellowstone from 1938] [] Historical poster of Yellowstone from 1938 Yellowstone National Park, set aside as a national park on March 1, 1872, is located mostly in the U.S. state of Wyoming, though it also extends into Montana and Idaho. The park was the first of its kind, and is known for its wildlife and its many geothermal features, especially Old Faithful Geyser, one of the most popular areas in the park. It has many types of ecosystems, but the Boreal forest is dominant. Aboriginal Americans have lived in the Yellowstone region for at least
