clueweb09-en0002-04-26897.0 Solid Earth [] [Skip to main content][Skip to navigation] Exploring the Yellowstone Geoecosystem A Digital Resource Collection for Teaching and Learning Integrating Research and Education > Yellowstone > Key Topics > Solid Earth Solid Earth This page was written by Denny Capps as part of the DLESE Community Services Project: Integrating Research in Education. [Old Faithful Geyser basin.] Old Faithful Geyser basin. Details Volcanism Resources describing Yellowstone volcanism in a solid earth context. [show]Show me information about volcanism [hide]Hide A Living, Breathing Caldera. This report describes the crustal deformation of the Yellowstone Hotspot from 1923 to 1995. Measurements show that the Yellowstone
clueweb09-en0002-04-26897.75 Solid Earth volcanism [hide]Hide A Living, Breathing Caldera. This report describes the crustal deformation of the Yellowstone Hotspot from 1923 to 1995. Measurements show that the Yellowstone Caldera underwent rapid uplift from 1923 to 1985; this was followed by ten years of subsidence. The report also summarizes the University of Utah's research program to monitor the caldera using GPS stations. Information on surrounding fault zones is also provided. (more info) Eastern Basin-Range and Yellowstone Hotspot GPS Network. This clearinghouse of GPS information focuses on the overall strain and deformation field of the Basin and Range Province that includes the Yellowstone volcanic system
