clueweb09-en0002-04-26891.75 Human Impacts and Hazards Facility. Details Volcanism Resources describing the impacts and hazards associated with Yellowstone volcanics. [show]Show me information about volcanism [hide]Hide A Living, Breathing Caldera. This report describes the crustal deformation of the Yellowstone Hotspot from 1923 to 1995. Measurements show that the Yellowstone Caldera underwent rapid uplift from 1923 to 1985; this was followed by ten years of subsidence. The report also summarizes the University of Utah's research program to monitor the caldera using GPS stations. Information on surrounding fault zones is also provided. (more info) Current Activity at the Yellowstone Volcanic System. This website provides a monthly summary of current
