clueweb09-en0004-31-10693.75 Volcano Hazards Program Features Archive erupt in the Aleutian Islands in three weeks. Okmok Volcano erupted unexpectedly and explosively on July 12, followed by Cleveland Volcano, 100 miles away, on July 21. Okmok erupts in Alaska [Okmok erupting] Okmok Volcano in Alaska started erupting on July 12 at 11:43 AKDT (19:43 UTC). The initial phase of the eruption was quite explosive and produced a wet, ash and gas-rich plume that reached 50,000 feet above sea level. Mount St. Helens Eruption Ceases, for now [Mount St. Helens dome] Scientists say the nearly three and a half years of eruption at Mount St. Helens is over for
